    id: 'exam-error-lv-kokko-251',
    title: '入試の正誤問題（国公立251：総合60）',
    points: ['「…すぎて〜できない」は程度の語と不定詞で表し、不定詞の目的語を重ねない。「十分に〜」の語は形容詞のうしろ、名詞の前に置く。形容詞を強める語の順序も確かめる。', '「とても〜なので」は節と、「…すぎて」は不定詞と組み合わせる。単数名詞を強めるときは強めの語、不定冠詞、形容詞、名詞の順に並べ、冠詞の形は次の語の音で決める。'],
    examples: [{ en: 'The suitcase was too heavy for my sister to carry, but she was strong enough to pull it along the platform.', ja: 'そのスーツケースは妹には重すぎて持ち上げられなかったが、ホームを引いて歩くだけの力は十分にあった。' }],
    questions: [
      { sentence: 'Yesterday evening the typhoon (A) was too violent that the ferry operator (B) called off all crossings to the island, and hundreds of tourists (C) were forced to stay (D) in hotels near the port overnight.', choices: ['(A) was too violent that', '(B) called', '(C) were forced to', '(D) in'], answer: 0, why: 'was too violent that を was so violent that とする。程度の語と、続く節や不定詞の組み合わせを混ぜない。' },
      { sentence: 'Although the volunteers (A) spent the entire weekend collecting donations, they (B) did not gather enough of food to feed every family in the shelter, so the city (C) promised to send (D) additional supplies on Monday.', choices: ['(A) spent', '(B) did not gather enough of food', '(C) promised', '(D) additional'], answer: 1, why: 'did not gather enough of food を did not gather enough food とする。この語は名詞の前に直接置き、前置詞を入れない。' },
      { sentence: 'The hotel (A) that my parents (B) booked for our trip seemed charming on its website, but we soon found that the guest rooms (C) were too much small for a family of five (D) with large suitcases.', choices: ['(A) that', '(B) booked', '(C) were too much small', '(D) with'], answer: 2, why: 'were too much small を were much too small とする。形容詞の程度を「あまりにも〜すぎる」と強めるときは、強めの語を「…すぎる」の語の前に置く。量を表す語を形容詞の直前に置く語順は誤りになる。' },
      { sentence: 'Because the lid (A) had been screwed on so tightly by the machine at the factory, my grandmother (B) asked me to help, but even I (C) found that it was too tight for me (D) to turn it.', choices: ['(A) had been', '(B) asked', '(C) found', '(D) to turn it'], answer: 3, why: 'to turn it を to turn とする。「…すぎて〜できない」の形では、不定詞の目的語にあたるものは文の主語と同じなので、不定詞のあとに代名詞の目的語をもう一度置くと重複になり誤りになる。' },
      { sentence: 'The documentary about rescue dogs told (A) so a touching story that several viewers around me (B) were quietly crying before the credits, and my friend (C) who usually dislikes such films said she (D) hoped to see it twice more.', choices: ['(A) so a touching story', '(B) were', '(C) who', '(D) hoped'], answer: 0, why: 'so a touching story を such a touching story とする。強めの語のあとは、不定冠詞、形容詞、名詞の順に並べる。' },
      { sentence: 'During my trip to an old castle town last spring, I (A) noticed that there (B) were too many traffic on the narrow lanes, and the town now (C) is planning to close (D) some of them to cars.', choices: ['(A) noticed', '(B) were too many traffic', '(C) is planning', '(D) some of'], answer: 1, why: 'were too many traffic を was too much traffic とする。名詞の種類に合わせて数や量を表す語を選ぶ。' },
      { sentence: 'Experts (A) say that most children are not physically ready for long-distance running until they (B) are about twelve, because before that age their bones (C) are not enough strong to handle the stress (D) of daily training.', choices: ['(A) say', '(B) are', '(C) are not enough strong to', '(D) of'], answer: 2, why: 'are not enough strong to を are not strong enough to とする。この語は形容詞や副詞のうしろに置く決まりである。' },
      { sentence: 'The judges (A) were impressed by the calm and confident way the young pianist (B) played, and the newspaper (C) later reported that her concert had attracted (D) quite an huge crowd for a classical event.', choices: ['(A) were', '(B) played', '(C) later', '(D) quite an huge crowd'], answer: 3, why: 'quite an huge crowd を quite a huge crowd とする。不定冠詞の形は次の語の最初の音で決まり、子音の音で始まる語の前では母音用の形は使わない。つづりが母音字で始まっても、発音が子音なら同じである。' },
      { sentence: 'The new rules were too complicated for most staff members (A) to follow them, which led the manager to (B) hold a meeting (C) in which she explained each point (D) slowly and then answered questions from everyone patiently.', choices: ['(A) to follow them', '(B) hold', '(C) in which', '(D) slowly'], answer: 0, why: 'to follow them を to follow とする。「…すぎて〜できない」の形では、不定詞の目的語にあたるものは文の主語と同じなので、不定詞のあとに代名詞の目的語をもう一度置くと重複になり誤りになる。' },
      { sentence: 'The small museum in our town (A) has struggled for years, and the director says it still (B) does not receive enough of support from the city (C) to repair its old roof (D) properly.', choices: ['(A) has', '(B) does not receive enough of support', '(C) to', '(D) properly'], answer: 1, why: 'does not receive enough of support を does not receive enough support とする。この語は限定詞のない名詞の前に直接置き、前置詞を入れない。' },
    ],
