    examples: [{ en: 'The reason the ferry was canceled is that strong winds were expected, and whoever booked a ticket can decide whether to take the next boat or ask for a refund.', ja: 'フェリーが欠航になった理由は強風が予想されたことであり、切符を予約した人はだれでも、次の船に乗るか払い戻しを求めるかを決めることができる。' }],
    questions: [
      { sentence: 'The memoir describes how the young author, newly arrived in a foreign city, would stand on street corners for hours trying to work out [which bus did he need], too shy to ask strangers and too proud to admit to his family that he was lost.', choices: ['which bus he needed', 'which bus needed he', 'which bus he did needed', 'he needed which bus'], answer: 0, why: 'which bus he needed を使う。疑問詞で始まる節が動詞の目的語になる間接疑問では、疑問文の倒置をせず、疑問詞の後ろを主語＋動詞の平叙文の語順にしなければならない。' },
      { sentence: 'Ecologists warn that a large part of [that] we currently know about coral reefs is based on a few well studied sites in shallow water, and that the deeper reefs, which are far harder to reach, may behave in ways that existing models fail to predict.', choices: ['what', 'which', 'that what', 'what that'], answer: 0, why: 'what を使う。後ろの節で動詞の目的語や主語が欠けているときは、「〜ということ」の接続詞ではなく、欠けた名詞を含んで「〜もの・こと」を表す関係詞を使う。' },
      { sentence: '[If] the ancient inscriptions record a spoken language or merely a system of accounting symbols remains a matter of fierce dispute among specialists, partly because so few examples have survived and partly because none of them is long enough to reveal a grammar.', choices: ['Whether', 'Whether if', 'If or not', 'What'], answer: 0, why: 'Whether を使う。「〜かどうか」の名詞節を文頭に置いて主語にするときは、条件の意味も持つ接続詞は使えず、「〜かどうか」専用の接続詞で節を始めなければならない。' },
      { sentence: 'The committee was persuaded by [the fact what] the proposed dam would flood several villages whose residents had worked the land there for generations, and so it advised the government to look elsewhere for a site that would displace far fewer people.', choices: ['the fact that', 'the fact which', 'the fact as that', 'the fact of'], answer: 0, why: 'the fact that を使う。名詞の内容を説明する同格の名詞節は「〜という」を表す接続詞で導く。後ろは名詞の欠けがない完全な文なので、関係代名詞や「〜もの」の関係詞は使えない。' },
      { sentence: 'When the research team at last arrived at the abandoned station on the frozen coast, they found a cupboard full of strange instruments and spent the evening debating [which to use it] first, because nobody in the group had received proper training before the trip.', choices: ['which to use', 'which using', 'which to use them', 'which should use'], answer: 0, why: 'which to use を使う。疑問詞の後ろに不定詞を続けて「何を〜すべきか」を表すとき、疑問詞がすでに不定詞の目的語の役割を果たしているので、動詞の後ろに目的語の代名詞を重ねない。' },
      { sentence: 'Although the letters had been carefully preserved by the family for over a century, the archivist admitted that she still had no idea [where had they been written], since none of them carried a date, an address, or even a clear reference to a particular town or season.', choices: ['where they had been written', 'where had been they written', 'where were they being written', 'where they had written been'], answer: 0, why: 'where they had been written を使う。疑問詞で始まる節が文の中に埋め込まれる間接疑問では、疑問文の倒置をせず、疑問詞の後ろを主語＋動詞の平叙文の語順にしなければならない。' },
      { sentence: 'Once the research expedition came back from the remote island, the sponsors agreed that [whatever the scientists had collected it] would be shared evenly by the national museum and the university, although several rare specimens were later sent abroad for further analysis.', choices: ['whatever the scientists had collected', 'what ever the scientists had collected it', 'whatever the scientists had collected them', 'whatever had the scientists collected'], answer: 0, why: 'whatever the scientists had collected を使う。「〜するものは何でも」を表す複合関係代名詞の節では、複合関係代名詞自体が欠けた目的語の役割を果たすので、動詞の後ろに代名詞を重ねてはいけない。' },
      { sentence: 'Doctors still disagree over a basic question, namely [if or not] a mild fever should be treated with medicine at all, since a moderate rise in body temperature may actually help the immune system fight off certain infections more effectively.', choices: ['whether or not', 'whether if or not', 'if whether or not', 'or not whether'], answer: 0, why: 'whether or not を使う。「〜かどうか」の接続詞の直後に「あるいはそうでないか」を続けられるのは専用の接続詞だけで、条件の意味も持つ接続詞の直後には続けられない。' },
      { sentence: 'Before revealing what the study had found, the lecturer paused for a moment and asked the audience [they guessed what] the volunteers had chosen when offered either a small reward immediately or a much larger one after waiting a full week.', choices: ['what they guessed', 'what did they guess', 'what they guessed did', 'did they guess what'], answer: 0, why: 'what they guessed を使う。考えや推測を表す動詞の目的語にあたる疑問詞は、その動詞の後ろに残さず節の先頭に出す。文の中に埋め込まれた節なので、その後ろは倒置せず主語＋動詞の語順にする。' },
      { sentence: 'Faced with conflicting reports from the front, the exhausted general had to choose [if to] retreat across the river before nightfall or to hold his position on the hills and wait for fresh reinforcements from the capital that might arrive at dawn.', choices: ['whether to', 'whether if to', 'if or not to', 'to whether'], answer: 0, why: 'whether to を使う。「〜すべきかどうか」を不定詞で表すときは、条件の意味も持つ接続詞の後ろに不定詞は続けられず、「〜かどうか」専用の接続詞の後ろに不定詞を置く。' },
    ],
